From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:50:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] KitKat UI P35: restore the 4.4 translucent nav bar
 gradient scrim

Re-wire the BarTransitions gradient machinery (vestigial since the
flat-color rewrite: mGradient/mGradientAlpha kept but never targeted)
into the per-bar 4.4 scrim: a bar flagged with the new
setGradientScrimEnabled(true) draws its gradient drawable at full
alpha over a fully transparent bar in MODE_SEMI_TRANSPARENT /
MODE_TRANSLUCENT, instead of the flat semi-transparent overlay.

NavigationBarTransitions opts in and swaps its gradient drawable
(nav_background.9.png, a solid black patch) for the new
nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml: a near-black gradient rising from the
bottom of the bar fading to transparent at the top - the 4.4
windowTranslucentNavigation look. The P9 opaque default is
unaffected; apps that ask for a translucent nav bar get the 4.4
scrim. PhoneStatusBarTransitions keeps the flat overlay.

Change-Id: Ia117f778659a019c541780dc5f6f30a7ae3cf07e
---
 .../res/drawable/nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml     | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../NavigationBarTransitions.java             |  8 +++++-
 .../statusbar/phone/BarTransitions.java       | 25 +++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml b/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..e528f33293ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/nav_bar_kitkat_scrim.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!--
+  ~ KitKat UI Project: the 4.4 translucent nav bar scrim. When an app asked
+  ~ for windowTranslucentNavigation, 4.4 made the bar fully transparent and
+  ~ drew a dark gradient rising from the bottom of the screen over the app
+  ~ content, instead of a flat translucent overlay. Used by
+  ~ NavigationBarTransitions via the BarTransitions gradient machinery.
